          "title": "Bierlachs",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Bierlachs is a fast German Skat variant, also called Beer Skat, played with a 32-card pack and point-trick scoring."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Bierlachs is a German social variant of Skat, also known as Beer Skat or Bierlatz. It keeps the 32-card Skat pack and point-trick core but compresses the hand into a short pub-game format where rapid card counting and cooperation matter immediately."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "3 players use the table arrangement described for Bierlachs."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card French or German Skat pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "32-card French or German Skat pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal from a 32-card Skat pack to three players, preserving the Skat-style rank order and trump logic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
